  <xs:element name="GetChangeOrder" type="GetChangeOrderType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>The purpose of the GetChangeOrder BOD is to query another business application or module for information about one or more ChangeOrder instances. The response is a ShowChangeOrder BOD.  The Get verb takes several parameters to constrain the data of interest including ChangeOrder identity and subset.</xs:documentation>
      <xs:documentation>Generally speaking, the Get verb plays the "Read" role in a CRUD data access layer.  Like SQL for a database, the Get verb allows for "selection" and "projection".  That is, data to return can be selected based on identity and values for other fields (the WHERE clause in SQL).  Matching data can be projected onto a specific set of fields of interest (the SELECT clause in SQL) to return.  However, the full expressiveness of SQL is not used.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
  </xs:element>
  <xs:complexType name="GetChangeOrderType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation>The purpose of the GetChangeOrder BOD is to query another business application or module for information about one or more ChangeOrder instances. The response is a ShowChangeOrder BOD.  The Get verb takes several parameters to constrain the data of interest including ChangeOrder identity and subset.</xs:documentation>
